{"id":"8e40fcb010a6d674d247ac04e749e35487cfd3cd","url":"https://github.com/JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback","title":"GitHub - JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback: Are you running too few agents, or too many? AgentPlayback visualizes your coding agents so you can see when each one ran, when it was blocked on you, and what it cost.","site_name":"Buzzing","source":"github.com","byline":null,"excerpt":"Are you running too few agents, or too many? AgentPlayback visualizes your coding agents so you can see when each one ran, when it was blocked on you, and what it cost. - JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback","content_html":"<DIV class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div data-hpc=\"true\" containertiming=\"hpc\"><article itemprop=\"text\">\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  A local visualization of your coding agents that shows you if you're running too many, or too few at a time.\n</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  <code>npx agentplayback</code>\n  &#160;&#160;or&#160;&#160;\n  <code>bunx agentplayback</code>\n</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641800306-ced4cec4-9668-42ad-ac6f-a8479a1fd903.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Dk-Gw5HkyqS5soZWYEMsBuVmdaDGIekFWVVdYee9bLU\"><img width=\"1220\" height=\"763\" alt=\"AgentPlayback theme transition\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641800306-ced4cec4-9668-42ad-ac6f-a8479a1fd903.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Dk-Gw5HkyqS5soZWYEMsBuVmdaDGIekFWVVdYee9bLU\" data-animated-image=\"\"></a>\n</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641805773-e4616758-5c83-476b-8b68-fc17dd62acb6.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..pR7NUaVm0bIbpUANtFC__8xRFuw3kF2cXrYt_y2hX-E\"><img width=\"1000\" height=\"563\" alt=\"AgentPlayback timeline\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641805773-e4616758-5c83-476b-8b68-fc17dd62acb6.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..pR7NUaVm0bIbpUANtFC__8xRFuw3kF2cXrYt_y2hX-E\" data-animated-image=\"\"></a>\n</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641807743-983b0d61-50bd-4b91-986a-dd06c8d536cc.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..S0V5Nr8DJpMukFHnUqxPksjqS19CfOA5lzgdRTaHCiI\"><img width=\"1493\" height=\"793\" alt=\"Frame 2147230025\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641807743-983b0d61-50bd-4b91-986a-dd06c8d536cc.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..S0V5Nr8DJpMukFHnUqxPksjqS19CfOA5lzgdRTaHCiI\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AgentPlayback reads existing Codex and Claude Code session logs and turns them into a visual timeline showing:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>When your agents are working versus waiting for your input</li>\n<li>Sessions grouped by task and project</li>\n<li>Time, token usage, and estimated cost</li>\n<li>Daily history across your agents</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Data is processed locally and stays local.</p>\n<P dir=\"auto\"><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Supported agents</h2><a id=\"user-content-supported-agents\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Supported agents\" href=\"#supported-agents\"></a></P>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AgentPlayback currently supports <strong>Codex</strong> and <strong>Claude Code</strong>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Contributions adding other agents are welcome. Please include screenshots verifying that the UI and data look right. The interface is intentionally opinionated, though, so integrations that require a substantially different presentation may be better maintained as forks.</p>\n<P dir=\"auto\"><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Run from source</h2><a id=\"user-content-run-from-source\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Run from source\" href=\"#run-from-source\"></a></P>\n<div dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"git clone https://github.com/JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback.git\ncd AgentPlayback\nnpm install\nnpm run build\nnpm start\"><pre>git clone https://github.com/JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback.git\n<span>cd</span> AgentPlayback\nnpm install\nnpm run build\nnpm start</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  Created by the makers of <a href=\"https://dayflow.so\" rel=\"nofollow\">Dayflow</a>.\n</p>\n</article></div></DIV>","content_text":"A local visualization of your coding agents that shows you if you're running too many, or too few at a time. npx agentplayback or bunx agentplayback AgentPlayback reads existing Codex and Claude Code session logs and turns them into a visual timeline showing: When your agents are working versus waiting for your input Sessions grouped by task and project Time, token usage, and estimated cost Daily history across your agents Data is processed locally and stays local. Supported agents AgentPlayback currently supports Codex and Claude Code. Contributions adding other agents are welcome. Please include screenshots verifying that the UI and data look right. The interface is intentionally opinionated, though, so integrations that require a substantially different presentation may be better maintained as forks. Run from source git clone https://github.com/JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback.git cd AgentPlayback npm install npm run build npm start Created by the makers of Dayflow.","fetched_at":"2026-08-27T17:36:54.106Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">\n  A local visualization of your coding agents that shows you if you're running too many, or too few at a time.\n</p>","sentences":[{"en":"A local visualization of your coding agents that shows you if you're running too many, or too few at a time.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">\n  <code>npx agentplayback</code>\n  &#160;&#160;or&#160;&#160;\n  <code>bunx agentplayback</code>\n</p>","sentences":[{"en":"npx agentplayback or bunx agentplayback","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">AgentPlayback reads existing Codex and Claude Code session logs and turns them into a visual timeline showing:</p>","sentences":[{"en":"AgentPlayback reads existing Codex and Claude Code session logs and turns them into a visual timeline showing:","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li>When your agents are working versus waiting for your input</li>","sentences":[{"en":"When your agents are working versus waiting for your input","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li>Sessions grouped by task and project</li>","sentences":[{"en":"Sessions grouped by task and project","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li>Time, token usage, and estimated cost</li>","sentences":[{"en":"Time, token usage, and estimated cost","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<li>Daily history across your agents</li>","sentences":[{"en":"Daily history across your agents","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">Data is processed locally and stays local.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Data is processed locally and stays local.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Supported agents</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"Supported agents","zh":"支持代理"}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">AgentPlayback currently supports <strong>Codex</strong> and <strong>Claude Code</strong>.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"AgentPlayback currently supports Codex and Claude Code.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">Contributions adding other agents are welcome. Please include screenshots verifying that the UI and data look right. The interface is intentionally opinionated, though, so integrations that require a substantially different presentation may be better maintained as forks.</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Contributions adding other agents are welcome.","zh":null},{"en":"Please include screenshots verifying that the UI and data look right.","zh":null},{"en":"The interface is intentionally opinionated, though, so integrations that require a substantially different presentation may be better maintained as forks.","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">Run from source</h2>","sentences":[{"en":"Run from source","zh":"从源代码运行"}]},{"html_en":"<p dir=\"auto\">\n  Created by the makers of <a href=\"https://dayflow.so\" rel=\"nofollow\">Dayflow</a>.\n</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Created by the makers of Dayflow.","zh":null}]}],"translated":true,"content_html_zh":"<div class=\"page\" id=\"readability-page-1\"><div data-hpc=\"true\" containertiming=\"hpc\"><article itemprop=\"text\">\n<p dir=\"auto\">A local visualization of your coding agents that shows you if you're running too many, or too few at a time.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">npx agentplayback or bunx agentplayback</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641800306-ced4cec4-9668-42ad-ac6f-a8479a1fd903.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Dk-Gw5HkyqS5soZWYEMsBuVmdaDGIekFWVVdYee9bLU\"><img width=\"1220\" height=\"763\" alt=\"AgentPlayback theme transition\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641800306-ced4cec4-9668-42ad-ac6f-a8479a1fd903.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..Dk-Gw5HkyqS5soZWYEMsBuVmdaDGIekFWVVdYee9bLU\" data-animated-image=\"\"></a>\n</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">\n  <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641805773-e4616758-5c83-476b-8b68-fc17dd62acb6.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..pR7NUaVm0bIbpUANtFC__8xRFuw3kF2cXrYt_y2hX-E\"><img width=\"1000\" height=\"563\" alt=\"AgentPlayback timeline\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641805773-e4616758-5c83-476b-8b68-fc17dd62acb6.gif?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..pR7NUaVm0bIbpUANtFC__8xRFuw3kF2cXrYt_y2hX-E\" data-animated-image=\"\"></a>\n</p>\n<a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641807743-983b0d61-50bd-4b91-986a-dd06c8d536cc.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..S0V5Nr8DJpMukFHnUqxPksjqS19CfOA5lzgdRTaHCiI\"><img width=\"1493\" height=\"793\" alt=\"Frame 2147230025\" src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/29084938/641807743-983b0d61-50bd-4b91-986a-dd06c8d536cc.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..S0V5Nr8DJpMukFHnUqxPksjqS19CfOA5lzgdRTaHCiI\"></a>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AgentPlayback reads existing Codex and Claude Code session logs and turns them into a visual timeline showing:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>When your agents are working versus waiting for your input</li>\n<li>Sessions grouped by task and project</li>\n<li>Time, token usage, and estimated cost</li>\n<li>Daily history across your agents</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Data is processed locally and stays local.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">支持代理</h2><a id=\"user-content-supported-agents\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Supported agents\" href=\"#supported-agents\"></a><p></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">AgentPlayback currently supports Codex and Claude Code.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Contributions adding other agents are welcome. Please include screenshots verifying that the UI and data look right. The interface is intentionally opinionated, though, so integrations that require a substantially different presentation may be better maintained as forks.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"></p><h2 tabindex=\"-1\" dir=\"auto\">从源代码运行</h2><a id=\"user-content-run-from-source\" aria-label=\"Permalink: Run from source\" href=\"#run-from-source\"></a><p></p>\n<div dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"git clone https://github.com/JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback.git\ncd AgentPlayback\nnpm install\nnpm run build\nnpm start\"><pre>git clone https://github.com/JerryZLiu/AgentPlayback.git\n<span>cd</span> AgentPlayback\nnpm install\nnpm run build\nnpm start</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Created by the makers of Dayflow.</p>\n</article></div></div>"}